// LN System — core Prisma schema.
//
// Reconstructed from the production database's own DDL (pg_dump), since the
// original schema.prisma was lost. Every table/column/type/constraint/index
// below mirrors the live database exactly; nothing here is speculative.
//
// Row Level Security is the real tenant-isolation boundary for this schema,
// not foreign keys: `companyId`/`branchId` columns on most tables are plain
// scalars with NO database foreign key (isolation is enforced by the
// `rls_company_match` / `rls_company_branch_match` policies in
// prisma/migrations/0_init/migration.sql, which Prisma has no syntax for).
//
// Every RLS-enabled table has BOTH `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` and `FORCE
// ROW LEVEL SECURITY` in that migration — Postgres exempts a table's OWNER
// from RLS unless FORCE is also set, and the role that runs `prisma migrate
// deploy` (and therefore owns every table it creates) is the same role the
// API connects as. Without FORCE, confirmed by direct testing against a
// real instance: RLS silently does nothing — full cross-tenant read AND
// write, even with zero session context set. This was the single biggest
// gap the pg_dump-based reconstruction missed (FORCE isn't visible in a
// plain `\dt`/schema browse, only by testing).
// A handful of tables (Branch, User, License, Role, Permission,
// InstallmentPolicy, Partner, AuditLog) DO carry a real companyId/branchId
// foreign key — that split is preserved exactly as found in the database,
// not normalized away.
//
// No `id` column has a database-level DEFAULT anywhere in the dump (no
// gen_random_uuid()/uuid_generate_v4()) — but `@default(uuid())` is a
// Prisma-side default (computed by the client before INSERT), which never
// shows up in pg_dump DDL either way. apps/api's code never supplies `id`
// on any `.create()` call, which only works if Prisma is generating it —
// confirmed by cross-referencing against the actual route/service code, so
// `@default(uuid())` was added to every `@id` field here despite the dump
// itself being silent on the question.

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

